  "transcript": [
    {
      "from": 0,
      "to": 20,
      "text": "Money has had the craziest glow in Indian history. I recently saw this billboard which shows the number of credit cards managed by Cred. We started with coins, actual metal. If you were rich, your pocket had a gym membership. Then came notes, suddenly wealth became portable. Then cards, which was basically society saying, trust me, I will pay you later."
    },
    {
      "from": 20,
      "to": 40,
      "text": "And then we did something ridiculous. We turned money into a sound. That's it. Today a ₹10 chai, a ₹1000 dinner and a ₹10,000 flight all begin with the same sound. The evolution wasn't going to cash or cash to card or card to QR codes. It was trust because somehow a country that used to count"
    },
    {
      "from": 40,
      "to": 44.950975,
      "text": "Not every rupee by hand, though trust a tiny scheme with its entire financial life."
    }
  ]
